        "original_id": "c11799a1-c48d-54e4-8f85-e20b2c6e06e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ibbi-Sipish, Ibbi-Zikir, Ibrium, Ishar-Damu, Irkab-Damu, Isar-Damu\n- Places: Ebla\n- Roles: vizier\n\nFacts:\n- In the 24th century BC, Ibrium, also spelled Ebrium, was the vizier of Ebla for king Irkab-Damu and his successor Isar-Damu.\n- Ibrium served as vizier for king Ishar-Damu for 15 years before his son.\n- In the 23rd century BC, Ibbi-Sipish, also called Ibbi-Zikir, was the vizier of Ebla for king Ishar-Damu for 17 years.\n- Ibbi-Sipish was the son and successor of Ibrium as vizier of Ebla.",
